---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Editorial standards"
  description="The sourcing, writing, correction, audio-rights, image-rights, and AI-assistance standards used by MelodyMind Knowledge."
  ><article class="reading-shell standards">
    <p class="eyebrow">Editorial standards</p><h1>
      Explain the mechanism. Show the source.
    </h1><h2>Research and claims</h2><p>
      Historical dates, technical descriptions, credits, quotations, and disputed origin
      claims require sources that directly support the wording. When reliable accounts
      disagree, the article names the disagreement instead of forcing a single answer.
    </p><h2>Writing</h2><p>
      Articles use clear American English and explain specialist vocabulary in context.
      Detail must help the reader hear, compare, or understand something specific. Generic
      significance claims, promotional adjectives, invented authority, and repeated
      summary paragraphs are removed during the mandatory anti-AI editorial pass.
    </p><h2>Original audio</h2><p>
      Interactive examples are produced for Knowledge without third-party samples unless a
      future article documents a separate license. Each example includes a plain-language
      listening description and a non-interactive fallback.
    </p><h2>Images</h2><p>
      Generated images are labeled as AI-generated editorial illustrations. They use
      anonymous contemporary subjects and are never presented as photographs of historical
      people or events.
    </p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>
      Substantive corrections receive a dated note. Quiet copy edits may improve clarity
      without changing the article's evidence or conclusion.
    </p>
  </article></Layout
>
<style>
  .standards {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .standards h1 {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .standards h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .standards p {
    font:
      1.08rem/1.7 Literata,
      Georgia,
      serif;
  }
</style>
